        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hugh Dancy, Will Graham, Hannibal Lecter, Thomas Harris, Mads Mikkelsen, Sarah Ann Birley, Jonathan Peter Dancy\n- Works: Hannibal, Oeuf, Red Dragon\n- Organizations: FBI\n- Roles: forensic psychiatrist, special investigator, professor, writer\n- Places: Stoke-on-Trent, Staffordshire, England\n\nFacts:\n- Hugh Dancy was born on 19 June 1975 in Stoke-on-Trent, Staffordshire, England.\n- Sarah Ann Birley, Hugh Dancy's mother, works in academic publishing.\n- Jonathan Peter Dancy, Hugh Dancy's father, is a Philosophy professor and writer.\n- The series Hannibal is based on characters and elements from Thomas Harris's novels Red Dragon and Hannibal.\n- Hannibal focuses on the relationship between FBI special investigator Will Graham, portrayed by Hugh Dancy, and Dr. Hannibal Lecter, portrayed by Mads Mikkelsen.\n- Dr. Hannibal Lecter is a forensic psychiatrist who is destined to become Will Graham's most cunning enemy.",
